      "textEn": "515\n\nHaving given the eyes to the Lord, tell me, O knower of the future. Yenakadeshedukkh sarvasargasthavam\nTvadiadrakram vayam madhudvishah. 21. Meaning of the word:\n\nCruel: Cruel; Tvam—you (formal); Akrur-samkhyaya—known by the name Akrur (meaning, one who is not cruel); Sm—certainly; Nah—our; Chakshuh—eyes; Hi—indeed; Dattam—given; Harase—are snatching; Bat—alas; Ajna—foolish; Vat—like; Yena—by whom; Eka—one; Deshe—in place; Akhil—all; Sarga—of creation; Saundhishtham—complete; Tvadiyam—yours; Adraatram—having seen; Vayam—we; Madhudvishah—enemies of the honey demon, Lord Krishna. Oh creator, although you have come here by the name of Akrur, you are cruel because you\nare taking away from us only those who are like fools, whom you once gave us—those eyes of ours\nfrom which we saw the completeness of your entire creation even in that one form of Lord Madhudvisha\nhave seen. Meaning: The gopis were not interested in looking at any object other than Krishna.\nTherefore, if Krishna leaves Vrindavan, then there will be no work left for his eyes. This\nkind of Krishna's departure was making the poor Gopis blind, and because of their sorrow, they were calling Akrur\nby whose name means \"not cruel,\" cruel. Those who are not delighted, those who are momentary, friends,\nThey do not examine themselves, they are always in the midst of their own misery. Having left, the king's son,\nWho was always with him, now became new and dear. 22). Meaning of the word\n\nNa—No; Nand-soonu—Son of Nanda Maharaj; Kshan—In a moment; Bhang—To break; Sauhridah—Of whose friendship; Srivikshite—\nThey see; Na—To us; Swa—By oneself; Kruta—Made; Aturaah—In one's control; Bata—Having left;\nGahen—Our houses; Swajanan—Relatives; Sutan—Children; Patin—Husbands; Tat—Towards that; Dasam—Slavery;\nAdhada—Directly; Upagataah—Accepted; Nav—New; Priyah—Lover. Hi! Nand's son, who breaks a loving friendship in an instant, will not be able to look at us directly.\nHe will not even be 