ीपुत्र, श्रीकृष्ण को।",
      "textEn": "516\n\nHappy dawn, the rain-shower, the giver of blessings.\nTruth will be revealed to the protected ones, surely. Yaah, the face of the one who is entered, of the king,\nThe smiling face of the one who is seen and the one who is heard. 23 ज़a. Meaning of the word\n\nSukham—happiness; Prabhat—morning; Rajani—night; Iyam—this; Ashishah—hopes; Satyah—truth; Bhavubhuvah—having become;\nPur—of the city; Yoshitam—of the women; Dhruvam—certainly; Yah—who; Sampravesya—entered;\nMukham—face; Vrajah-patih—the lord of Vraja; Pasyanti—will drink; Apangah—tilted; Utkalit—spread out; Smitah—\nlaughter; Asavam—nectar. The dawn that follows this night will surely be auspicious for the women of Mathura. Now all their hopes will be fulfilled because as soon as the Brahmapati enters their city, they\nwill be able to drink the nectar of the smile emanating from the crooked gaze of their face. For a moment, with the speech of the honey-bee-like,\nWith a concentrated mind, even the best of men.\nHow does the mighty one again appear?\nThe village women, with shy smiles, are confused. 24). Meaning of the words:\n\nTasam—their; Mukunda—Krishna; Madhu—like honey; Manju—sweet; Bhashita-him—by speech; Ghrutit-him—held; Chittah—mind;\nParavan-him—subject; Manaswi-him—intelligent; Api-him—even though; Katham-him—how; Punah-him—again; Nah-him—us; Pratyasayate-him—is captivated;\n\nAbalah-him—O children; Gramya-him—rural; Sa-lajj-him—shy; Smita-him—smiling; Vibhramai-him—by enchantment; Bhraman-him—been mesmerized..\n\nOh Gopis, although our Mukunda is intelligent and very obedient to his parents,\n\nBut once, after being charmed by the honey-like sweet words of the women of Mathura and being captivated by their\nattractive, lovely smiles, why did he ever return to us, the ignorant, rural, helpless women?\nThen why did he ever return? Now, the Dhruva will be seen there.\nThe food of the ten kings, the darkness, the darkness, the sattvicness.\nThe festival is the abode of the virtues of Shri Rama,\nThey who see the sound of the son of Devaki. 25. Meaning of the word\n\nAdya—today; Dhruvam—certainly; Tatra—there; Drishah—for the eyes; Bhavishyate—will be; Dasharha-bhoja-andhaka-vrishni-\nSatvatam—Dasharha, Bhoja, Andhaka, Vrishni, and the members of the Satvata dynasty; Maha-utsahah—great celebration; Shri—of Lakshmiji;\nRamanam—beloved; Guna—of all divine qualities; Aapadham—storehouse; Drakshyanti—will see; Ye—who; Cha—also; Adhwani—path\nPar; Devaki-putram—Devakiputra, to Srikrishna."
