      "textEn": "519\n\nEven if we do, we can live peacefully knowing that Krishna is living in our village.\nare living. Some of our friends who have not been imprisoned, they will cleverly find a way to bring Krishna's leftovers to us,\nand we will be able to stay alive. But if Krishna is not stopped, then we\nwill surely die.\"\n\nYesyanuragalalitasmitavallugamantra-\nLilavalokaparirambhanarasagustham. Neeta: Sm nah kshanamiva kshanada vina tamam\nGopyaah katham nvatitareem tamo durantam. 29). Meaning of the word\n\nYasya—Of whom; Anurag—With affection; Lalita—Beautiful; Smita—(where) there was laughter; Vallu—Attractive; Mantra—Mixed;\nConversation; Leela—Full of play; Avaloka—By looking; Parirambha—And embracing; Raas—Of Rasanritya; Goshthaam—To the group;\nNitaah sma—Laid down; Nah—For us; Kshanam—A moment; Iva—Like; Kshanada—At night; Vina—Without; Tam—His; Gopiya—Oh\nGopis; Katham—How; Nu—Undoubtedly; Atitarem—We will cross over; Tamah—Darkness; Durantam—Difficult.\n.\n\nWhen they brought us to a gathering of Raas dance where we enjoyed their affectionate and charming smiles,\ntheir delightful secret talks, their playful glances, and their embraces,\nwe reveled in it, then we spent many nights that felt like just a moment. Hey Gopis, so\nhow can we cross the insurmountable darkness of their absence? Meaning: The Gopis spent a long time with Krishna, like a moment, and in their absence, a moment seemed like an extremely long time. Yoahrah, the one who is always with the endless friend, the one who is like a broken sword among the cows.\n"
