      "textEn": "523\n\nTatropasprushya paniyam pitya mrishtam maniprabham. Vrikshashanmupavrajya saramo rathamavishat. 39. Meaning of the word:\nTatra—there; upasprashya—by touching water; peeyajal—in one's hand; peetva—by drinking; mrishtam—sweet; mani—like gems;\nTulya—equal; prabham—radiant; vriksha—of trees; shandam—grove; upavrajya—by walking near; sa-ramah—with Balarama; ratham—in the chariot;\nAavishat—became riders. The river's sweet water was sharper than the glittering jewels. Lord Krishna, for purification,\nwashed with water and performed Achamana (ritual purification) by taking it in his hand. Thereafter, he brought his chariot to a\ntree grove and, along with Balram, mounted it again. Akrurastavupamantrya nivashya cha rathoparipari. Having entered the lotus-like heart, he performed the prescribed bath. 40. Meaning of the word:\nAkrurah—Akrur; Tau—from both of them; Upamantryya—with permission; Nivishtaya—by seating them; Cha—and; Rath-Upari—on the chariot;\nKalindyah—of Yamuna; Hridam—in the pond; Aagatya—going; Snanam—bathing; Vidhi-vat—according to the scriptural method;\nAcharat—completed.\nAkrur asked both the brothers to sit on the chariot. Thereafter, taking permission from them, they\nwent to Yamuna Kund and bathed according to the prescribed method in the scriptures. Nimajya Tasminslile Japam Brahmam Sanatanam. Tavev dadrasehakrooro Ramakrishnaau samanvitau. 41. Meaning of the word\n\nNimajjya—entering; Tasmin—in that; Salile—in water; Japam—while uttering; Brahma—Vedic mantra; Sanatanam—eternal; Tau—both of them; Ev—indeed; Dadrase—seen; Akrurah—Akrur; Ram-Krishnaau—Ram and Krishna; Samanvitau—together..\nEntering the water, while chanting the eternal mantras from the Vedas, Akrur suddenly saw Balram and\nKrishna in front of him. Ta Rathasthaau kathamih sutaanakadundubheha. Then, having not been able to speak, he was stunned. 42. There also, as before, he is again. I have seen the vision of the deceitful, but in what a flood of water. 43. Lex