nचारुप्रसन्नवदनं चारुहासनिरीक्षणम् ।\nसुभ्रून्नसं चारुकर्णं सुकपोलारुणाधरम् ॥ ४७॥\nप्रलम्बपीवरभुजं तुङ्गांसोरःस्थलश्रियम् ।\nकम्बुकण्ठं निम्ननाभिं वलिमत्पल्लवोदरम् ॥ ४८ ॥\n\nशब्दार्थ\n\nतस्य—उस (अनन्त शेष) की; उत्सङ्गे—गोद में; घन—वर्षा के बादल की तरह; श्यामम्—गहरा नीला; पीत—पीला;\nकौशेय—रेशमी; वाससम्—वस्त्र; पुरुषम्—परमेश्वर को; चतुः-भुजम्—चार भुजाओं वाले; शान्तम्—शान्त; पद्म—कमल",
      "textEn": "524\n\nThus, both of them; Rathastha—seated on the chariot; Katham—how; Iha—here; Sutau—both sons; Aanakadundubheh—of Vasudeva; Tarhi—therefore;\nThen; Swit—what; Syandane—on the chariot; Na Sthit—not being; Iti—thinking thus; Unmajjya—descending from the water; Vyachashta—seen;\nEv—indeed; Sah—He; Nyamajjat—entered the water; Darshanam—sight; Yat—if; Me—mine; Mrisha—false; Kim—perhaps;\nSalila—in the water; Tayorah—of both of them. Akrur thought: \"How can the two sons of Anakadundubhi, who are sitting on the chariot here in the water,\nstand up?\" Surely, he must have left the chariot.\"But when they came out of the river,\nthey were both on the chariot as before. While asking this question to himself, that \"Was the vision of them that I had in the water an illusion?\"\" Akrur again entered the pond. Even there, he saw the great lord, who was playing. Siddhacharanagandharvaisurairnatakandharaih. 44). Sahasrarsham deve sahasrapanamoulinam.\nBlue, white, and white-colored, situated like a white-colored bee. 45. Meaning of the word\n\nBhooyah - again; Tatra api - at that place; Saha - he; Adrakit - saw; Stuyamanam - praised; Ahi-Ishwaram - of the snakes\nSwami (the eternal serpent, who is the offspring of Balarama and is the bed of Vishnu); Siddha-charana-Gandharvaibhah - of the Siddhas, By Charanas and\nBy Gandharvas; Asuras - and by Asuras; Nat - bowed; Kandharas - from necks; Sahasra - thousands; Shirasam - with heads; Devam - to the God; Sahasra - thousands; Phana - from necks; Maulinam - and crown; Neel - blue; Ambaram - garments; Vis - lotus-nails; Tantu-like; Shwetam - white; Shrunga - with peaks; Shwetam - Mount Kailash; Iva - like; Sthitam - established..\n\nNow Akrur saw Sarpraj Anant Shesh there, whose praise was being done by Siddha, Charan, Gandharva and\n\nAsurgan were bowing their heads. Akrur saw the God who had\nthousands of heads, thousands of tails, and thousands of crowns.\nHis blue garment and the fibers of the lotus stem-\nLike a white-golden complexion, it seemed as if it were a white Kailash mountain with many peaks. Tasya utsanga ghanashyamam peethikauceyavasasam. The man, four-armed, peaceful, with lotus-like eyes. 46. Charuprasannavadanam charuhasanirikshanam. Subhrunnasam charukarnam sukapolarunadharam. 47). Pralambaparibhūjam tungāṃsōrāḷasthalaśriyam. Kambukantham, nimnaabhim, valimatpallavam, udaram. 48. Meaning of the word:\n\nTasya—of that (infinite); utsanga—in the lap; ghana—like rain clouds; shyamam—dark blue; peetam—yellow;\nKausheya—of silk; vasasam—cloth; purusham—to God; chatuh-bhujam—with four arms; shantam—peaceful; padma—lotus"
